From ab589bf80b669c9671b53573d489b6c6c45779ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 12:59:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] test: the real custodian daemon startup and
 direct-ingress path spellings

custody-v2-daemon-startup runs the REAL custody/v2/daemon.mjs main, bundled
the way the image bundles it with the original vault's production measured
config. Only the chip is stubbed (snpkey derive returns a test key) and every
fetch other than the host's is refused. Against a host /state server:
- 503, 500, 403, 401, a disconnect, a redirect, an empty or truncated 200, a
  blob sealed by another key, a tampered blob, an oversize body and a stall:
  the daemon does not start and writes nothing; the stored state is untouched.
- The stored state opens, and opens again after those failures.
- An explicit 404 whose first write fails starts nothing.
- An explicit 404 seals a fresh identity with the chip key before anything else.
At c95dcd3a, and with a mutant of a5eae96c's wiring that maps read errors to
"missing", a 503 writes a new identity over the stored state; both fail this
test.

custody-direct-ingress-paths puts the REAL Caddy (CADDY_BIN) and the generated
ingress in front of the REAL custodian router. 25 spellings of the
host-binding route (case, slashes, dot segments plain and %-encoded,
backslashes, encoded separators, double encoding, ;params, query, absolute
form) and the host's private routes never reach setHostSig or the guest port.
A mutant ingress forwarding /v2/custody/* lets 11 spellings through and fails.
